{
  "info": {
    "name": "MCDSS - Phase 7 (Assignment / Optimization ILP)",
    "description": "Exercises every Phase 7 (Assignment and Optimization / ILP) deliverable from TEAM_DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md against a running `docker compose up -d` stack: JB's FastAPI `POST /run-assignment` solver (and its Laravel wrapper `POST /api/assignment-runs` / `GET /api/assignment-runs/{id}`), plus the internal faculty workload allocation variant `POST /run-faculty-workload`.\n\nBuilds one end-to-end fixture (1 position with 1 slot + 2 scored applicants) so the assignment ILP has a real binding constraint to solve (only the higher `total_wsm_score` applicant should be assigned), then a second fixture (1 internal faculty + 1 course + expertise score) for the workload ILP.\n\nPrereqs:\n1. `docker compose up -d --build`\n2. `docker compose exec laravel php artisan migrate --seed` (requires the Phase 7 migrations for `assignment_runs`, `assignment_results`, `faculty_workload`, `courses`, `faculty_load_limits`, `faculty_expertise_scores` -- added 2026-07-18).\n3. Run once: `docker compose exec laravel php artisan tinker --execute=\"echo App\\Models\\Department::first()->id;\"` and paste the UUID into the `department_id` collection variable.\n4. Run once: `docker compose exec laravel php artisan tinker --execute=\"echo App\\Models\\HiringRound::first()->id;\"` (seeded by HiringRoundSeeder) and paste the UUID into the `hiring_round_id` collection variable.\n5. Run the whole collection top-to-bottom via Collection Runner (order matters). Section 3 requires ONE MORE manual tinker step mid-run -- see the description on '3.6 Seed Course & Expertise Fixtures (manual prereq)'.\n\nNote on scope: `POST /run-faculty-workload` has no Laravel-side wrapper in the current implementation (unlike `/run-assignment`, which is proxied through `POST /api/assignment-runs`) -- it is called directly against FastAPI with the `X-Service-Key` header, same as JB's `/parse-resume` testing pattern from Phase 4. There is also no `GET` endpoint for `faculty_workload` results (the plan does not define one), so the final persistence check in section 3 is a manual tinker verification, not an assertable API call -- flagged the same way Phase 3's forced-password-reset gap was flagged.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
