              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{admin_token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/user",
            "description": "There is no CRUD API for `courses`, `faculty_load_limits`, or `faculty_expertise_scores` in the current implementation (Person 4's tables have no Laravel controllers) -- this is the one manual DB step this collection needs. Copy `internal_applicant_profile_id` from the previous response, then run (uses single-quoted --execute with double-quoted PHP strings on purpose -- no backslashes anywhere, so nothing gets mangled if this gets copy-pasted through a markdown renderer):\n\n  docker compose exec laravel php artisan tinker --execute='\n  $courseCode = \"CS701-ILP\";\n  $course = DB::table(\"courses\")->where(\"course_code\", $courseCode)->first();\n  if (!$course) {\n      $courseId = DB::table(\"courses\")->insertGetId([\n          \"department_id\" => App\\Models\\Department::first()->id,\n          \"course_code\" => $courseCode,\n          \"course_name\" => \"Phase 7 ILP Test Course\",\n          \"units\" => 3,\n          \"semester\" => \"1st Semester\",\n          \"academic_year\" => 2026,\n          \"sections_required\" => 1,\n          \"is_active\" => true,\n          \"created_at\" => now(),\n      ], \"id\");\n  } else {\n      $courseId = $course->id;\n  }\n  $profileId = \"PASTE_internal_applicant_profile_id_HERE\";\n  DB::table(\"faculty_load_limits\")->updateOrInsert(\n      [\"applicant_profile_id\" => $profileId],\n      [\"max_units\" => 6, \"updated_at\" => now()]\n  );\n  DB::table(\"faculty_expertise_scores\")->updateOrInsert(\n      [\"applicant_profile_id\" => $profileId, \"course_id\" => $courseId],\n      [\"expertise_score\" => 0.85, \"created_at\" => now()]\n  );\n  echo $courseId;\n  '\n\nPaste the echoed UUID into the 'course_id' collection variable. The course insert is idempotent (safe to re-run across collection runs); the faculty rows are keyed to whatever internal_applicant_profile_id you captured this run, so re-running the earlier steps and this tinker script together is safe too. max_units=6 >= course units=3 so the workload ILP's capacity constraint is satisfiable, and sections_required=1 with exactly one eligible faculty candidate means the solver's equality constraint (each course gets exactly sections_required faculty) is satisfiable too -- both matter, since solve_faculty_workload() in main.py uses a hard `== sections_required` constraint, not '<='."
          },
